:: StoryInit
/* The Lamp at Saltmere, as a SugarCube story: a tiny fixture written for Inkventure (MIT). Built into
   lamp-sugarcube.html by scripts/fixtures/build-twine.ts. Walkthrough: take the can, climb, fill, light. */
<<set $hasCan to false>>
<<set $filled to false>>

:: Landing Stage
The ferry leaves you on the landing stage of Saltmere. Night is falling, and the lighthouse above the harbour is dark.

A paraffin can stands by the bollard.

<<link "Take the paraffin can" "Foot of the Tower">><<set $hasCan to true>><</link>>
[[Walk up to the lighthouse|Foot of the Tower]]

:: Foot of the Tower
The lighthouse door is ajar. A spiral stair climbs into the dark.<<if $hasCan>> The paraffin can sloshes in your hand.<</if>>

[[Climb the stair|Lamp Room]]
[[Wait for morning|The Lamp Stays Dark]]

:: Lamp Room
The great lamp sits in its brass cradle, its reservoir <<if $filled>>full of paraffin<<else>>dry<</if>>.

<<if $hasCan and not $filled>><<link "Fill the lamp" "Lamp Room">><<set $filled to true>><</link>><</if>>
<<if $filled>>[[Light the lamp|The Lamp Is Lit]]<</if>>
[[Go back down|Foot of the Tower]]

:: The Lamp Is Lit
The wick catches, and the beam sweeps out over the water. Far off, a ship's horn answers.

''THE END'': you have lit the lamp.

:: The Lamp Stays Dark
You sit on the step and wait. No ship will find the harbour tonight.

''THE END'': the lamp stays dark.
